# Source Curation Agent Prompt — Standard Template
# For converting old-grammar source blocks to new phi grammar.
#
# OLD GRAMMAR → NEW GRAMMAR
#
# FIELD FORMAT (exactly 9 whitespace-separated parts):
#   field <key> <name> <kernel_name> <force_name> <unit> <tau> <absorption> <advection>
#   kernel_name: inverse-square | gaussian-inverse-square | gaussian-inverse | erfc | exponential-decay | patch-levy
#   force_name: em | gravity | acoustic | seismic-body | seismic-surface | thermal | diffusion | advective
#   tau: f64 > 0.0
#   absorption: f64
#   advection: f64
#
# FORCE→KERNEL DEFAULT MAPPING:
#   em → inverse-square
#   gravity → inverse-square
#   acoustic → gaussian-inverse-square
#   seismic-body → gaussian-inverse-square
#   seismic-surface → erfc
#   thermal → exponential-decay
#   diffusion → gaussian-inverse-square
#   advective → patch-levy
#
# FRAME CONVERSION:
#   old: lat X lon Y [alt Z] → new: on earth X Y [Z]  (default X=0 if no alt)
#   old: pos lat_key lon_key alt_key scale → new: map+map extract (leave pos as comment)
#   old: source <name> → DISCARD — the "source" keyword does NOT exist in new grammar. 
#        The "url" line naturally starts a new block via flush!().
#
# TAU ESTIMATION:
#   If old block has explicit "tau N": use it.
#   Otherwise: source TTL / 10.  Minimum tau: 1.0.
#   For sources with quickly-changing data (ISS, weather): tau = min(TTL/10, 1.0).
#   For stable sources (star catalogs, geology): tau = TTL.
#
# FORCE GATE (must apply before conversion):
#   Litmus test: could a non-human organism evolve a sensory organ for this measurement?
#   − Stock prices, indices, economic data → DECLINE (no physical force)
#   − Bare counts without individual events → DECLINE
#   − Station lists, catalogs, registries → DECLINE
#   − Model forecasts (GFS, ECMWF reanalysis) → DECLINE
#   − Text warnings, alerts, weather text → DECLINE
#   + Radar, lidar, optical → PASS (EM)
#   + Seismometer, hydrophone → PASS (acoustic, seismic)
#   + Magnetometer, particle detector → PASS (EM)
#   + Thermometer, bolometer → PASS (thermal)
#   + Chemical sensor, gas chromatograph → PASS (diffusion, advective)
#   + Gravimeter → PASS (gravity)
#
# OUTPUT RULES:
#   1. One clean block per accepted source. No # comments, no markdown.
#   2. url starts the block (parser's flush!() triggers on url keyword)
#   3. Frame (on/at) must be present or flush refuses the block
#   4. All field lines in one contiguous block
#   5. Declined blocks → written to phi/dead_sources.φ
#   6. Accepted blocks → written to phi/sources_live.φ (or agent output file if batch)
#   7. Known parser limitations: header values cannot contain spaces (parser splits on whitespace)
#
# CURATION NOTES (separate file: batch_N_notes.φ):
#   For each block, write:
#   # Block N: <old_source_name> → ACCEPT|DECLINE <reason>
#   # Kernel: <choice> <rationale>
#   # Force Gate: <pass/fail> <explanation>
#   # Frame: <choice>
#   # Unit: <choice>
#   # Tau: <value> <rationale>
#   # Parser concerns: <any issues>
